<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Idris I al-Muta'ayyad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1039</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Idris ibn Ali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Idris I al-Muta'ayyad was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammudid-dynasty">Hammudid dynasty</a>, Arab descendants of the Idrisids who claimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> after the collapse of Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. He succeeded his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-ibn-ali">Yahya ibn Ali</a> al-Mutali as ruler of Málaga, the Hammudid base, in 1035, and also held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a>, until his death in 1039.</p></div>
